Sakura wallpaper
================

The same stretch of the Meguro river in Tokyo, by day and by night. Plasma
picks between them automatically: contents/images is used with a light colour
scheme, contents/images_dark with a dark one.

Light  "Cherry blossom trees in full bloom over a canal with pink lanterns"
       Crystal Kay (@xtalkay)
       https://unsplash.com/photos/7viWpO0fNss

Dark   "A canal bordered by cherry blossom trees", Meguro river
       Sora Sagano
       https://unsplash.com/photos/8sOZJ8JF0S8

Licence for both: Unsplash License -- https://unsplash.com/license

The Unsplash License permits commercial use and redistribution without
permission or attribution. Attribution is recorded here anyway: it costs
nothing, and a distribution that cannot say where its assets came from is a
distribution nobody can audit.

The shipped files are resized and cropped from the originals.

The day photograph is 16:9; its 16:10 and 4:3 variants are cropped toward the
top of the frame, because the subject is the blossom canopy and a centre crop
lands on empty canal.

The night photograph is 3:2, so every 16:9 variant loses some top and bottom.
Those are cropped centred, because the canal runs down the middle of that
frame with the lanterns either side of it.
